    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/493312380/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """was so fascinated with Van Horn, a man of 60 in perfect condition who never sleeps more than four hours. He built the Canadian Pacific, and is now railroading Cuba. He owns and runs hotels everywhere, countless model farms, paints, has a huge collection, knows Japanese pottery to the ground, is full of fun and spirits - a real Eponymous Hero.
Thursday Dec. 10. 03. Plaza Hotel. N. Y. 
Bernhard startled me by asking whether he should let it be known that he would be willing to succeed Cesnola as director of the Museum here. I saw a thousand advantages in it, but I do think it would be a waste of a man who can think. Today’s visit there confirmed me. It is a vast collection of horrors.
We went out after lunch to Brooklyn """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 110 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1903-04> .

